<blockquote>
<p>Hello. This is the <strong>Minimalist BHL Theme.</strong> Originally meant for <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/pedagon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5903100); return false;"><img class="small" src="/o/291d4f91f779a17af1d93889b31ec5261f087cdbb52ba4cb9c514f743d97ae14" alt="Pedagon" style="background-image:url("/o/6700e29a4a13614fdd8b18d472aa3351bcd0d29d1d5672a66261caa6872df970")" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/pedagon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5903100); return false;">Pedagon</a></span> for his use in his Department of Sciences articles, it has been changed to be more user-friendly. To include it, please use the following code:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[[include :scp-wiki:theme:black-highlighter-theme]]<br />
[[include :scp-wiki:theme:minimalist-bhl]]</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>&quot;But, I think this theme looks cool and I want to use it for Departments and other things!&quot;</em> Well, good news for you &#8212; you can! Just include the following code after the above snippet to edit the Header:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[[module CSS]]<br />
:root {<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;</span> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">--header-title:&#32;&quot;title&#32;here&quot;;</span><br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;</span> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">--header-subtitle:&#32;&quot;subtitle&#32;here&quot;;</span><br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;</span> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">--lgurl:&#32;url('your&#32;url&#32;here');</span><br />
}<br />
[[/module]]</p>
</blockquote>
</blockquote>
